    "_meanings": [
        "¦ {%m.%}\n <ab>N.</ab> of a powerful monkey-chief. [He was the son\n of Añjanā by the god Wind or Marut and hence called Māruti. He is represented\n as a monkey of extraordinary strength and prowess which he manifested\n on several critical occasions on behalf of Rāma whom he regarded as the\n idol of his heart. When Sītā was carried off by Rāvaṇa, he crossed\n the sea and brought news about her to his lord. He played a very important\n part in the great war at Laṅkā.]\n"
